---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility — AgentSutra"
  description="AgentSutra accessibility commitments, current design standards and known limits."
  canonicalPath="/accessibility/"
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-intro__grid shell">
      <p class="page-intro__context">Publication policy</p>
      <div>
        <h1>Accessibility</h1><p class="page-intro__lead">
          The lesson is not complete if the format prevents someone from reaching it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Our target</h2>
      <p>
        AgentSutra targets WCAG 2.2 Level AA for the canonical website and applies the same
        principles to social adaptations wherever each platform permits.
      </p>
      <h2>Built into the system</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Semantic headings, landmarks, lists and descriptive links.</li>
        <li>Keyboard operation, visible focus and a skip link.</li>
        <li>Text reflow at 320 CSS pixels and resilience at 400% zoom.</li>
        <li>Strong contrast, reduced-motion support and forced-colour support.</li>
        <li>A visible ordered text equivalent beside every Thread diagram.</li>
        <li>No essential meaning conveyed by colour, position or shape alone.</li>
        <li>Useful pages without client-side JavaScript or external fonts.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Testing does not equal perfection</h2>
      <p>
        Automated checks catch only part of the experience. Releases also require keyboard, zoom,
        screen-reader-informed, print and cross-browser review. Conformance is a maintained target,
        not a permanent badge.
      </p>
      <h2>Report a barrier</h2>
      <p>
        Use the correction channel listed on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.
        Include the page, device or assistive technology, and what prevented completion.
        Accessibility reports receive publication-priority review.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
